<title>USA: U.S. to continue China's MFN status, Qian says.</title>
<headline>U.S. to continue China's MFN status, Qian says.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chinese Foreign Minister Qian Qichen said Tuesday he believed the United States would maintain China's Most Favored Nation (MFN) trading status.</p>
<p>&quot;I believe that the U.S. government has the determination to maintain the MFN status,&quot; Qian told reporters through an interpreter after meeting National Security Adviser Sandy Berger at the White House.</p>
</text>
